<p>
  Agentic tasks see the largest gains because agent trajectories involve multi-turn interactions
  with tool calls, where the model often generates high-entropy "thinking" tokens interspersed with
  deterministic structured outputs. The high-entropy tokens that previously dragged down target-only
  acceptance are exactly where rejection sampling + TV loss shines — the draft tracks the target
  distribution well regardless of how spread-out it is.
</p>
<p>
  The key practical result: <strong>one pre-RL training phase with e2e TV loss</strong> is sufficient.
  No online MTP updating during RL. No extra memory for MTP optimizer states. No gradient interference
  with the backbone policy. The MTP module is frozen during all of RL training, yet acceptance rates
  remain stable throughout — because TV training has already made the draft entropy-invariant.
</p>
</section>

